  "mechanisms": [
    "Spatial information is stored hierarchically.",
    "Spatial relations between any two locations are stored explicitly only if those locations are within the same superordinate unit.",
    "Spatial relations not stored explicitly are inferred by combining the relations from between and within superordinate units.",
    "The inference process may weight higher-level information more heavily than lower-level information.",
    "Distortions arise because the level of processing necessary for precise encoding or inference is typically not performed."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "Superordinate direction (East-West vs. North-South)",
    "Amount of stimulus deviation from superordinate direction (15, 45, 75 degrees)"
  ],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "The way people encode spatial information is critically influenced by higher-order organizational structure, which causes systematic errors in judgments about spatial relationships."
  ],
  "domains": [
    "A3_Spatial_Config",
    "A9_Task_Cognition"
  ],
